<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<form name="frmWoD20th" formType="sheetTemplate" dataType="AndreOliveira.Styllern.WoD20th" title="World of Darkness 20th Anniversary Edition" align="client" theme="dark">
	<script>
		<![CDATA[
			-- Every field write this sheet makes to ITSELF goes through here (SPEC V122).
			--
			-- Writing a value that is already there is not free: it wakes every dataLink on
			-- that field and every renderer hanging off them, and those renderers write more
			-- fields. The renderers below run on load and on both switches, so the same value
			-- was being written back dozens of times per open and each write bought a whole
			-- cascade - which is what froze the sheet on a saved character (SPEC B34).
			--
			-- Four lines, in one place, so the gate has one thing to check instead of every
			-- assignment in the file.
			-- ---- PICKER_LIST (SPEC I27, 68th round) ------------------------------------------
			--
			-- Every picker list the sheet offers, declared ONCE, keyed by FIELD ROOT. It used to
			-- live inline in each template's items=/values=, which meant the twenty-five ritual
			-- combos each carried their own copy of the same 284 names - 480,053 bytes of pure
			-- duplication in the compiled .lfm.lua (SPEC R92d).
			--
			-- On the ROOT and not per form (SPEC I27 rule 1): WoD20.1 and WoD20.2 carry no <script> at
			-- all, and four of these lists live in them. The root script is parsed before any
			-- <import>, the same reason the health track sits here.
			--
			-- items and values are ONE list: the authored pair was identical for all eleven
			-- declarations (measured). pickerItems writes values from it and items from it after
			-- the era/language pass, which is what keeps the pair aligned (SPEC V202).
			--
			-- CONSTANT: nothing writes into these tables (SPEC V201). One table_remove here would
			-- poison every combo that shares it, and there is no authored copy left to recover
			-- from - that is what the second leg of V201 forbids.
			PICKER_LIST = {
				-- >>> PICKER_LIST_BEGIN (SPEC V211b - the gate finds this region by MARKER)
				["clan"] = {
					"", "Assamite", "Brujah", "Followers of Set", "Gangrel", "Giovanni", "Lasombra", "Malkavian",
					"Nosferatu", "Ravnos", "Toreador", "Tremere", "Tzimisce", "Ventrue", "Baali", "Blood Brothers",
					"Daughters of Cacophony", "Harbingers of Skulls", "Kiasyd", "Nagaraja", "Salubri", "Samedi",
					"True Brujah", "Ahrimanes", "Anda", "Cappadocians", "Lamia", "Lhiannan", "Noiad", "Assamite Antitribu",
					"Brujah Antitribu", "City Gangrel", "Country Gangrel", "Malkavian Antitribu", "Nosferatu Antitribu",
					"Ravnos Antitribu", "Salubri Antitribu", "Serpents of the Light", "Toreador Antitribu",
					"Tremere Antitribu", "Assamite Sorcerers", "Assamite Viziers", "Daitya", "Tlacique", "Warrior Setites",
					"Mariners", "Lasombra Antitribu", "Dominate Malkavians", "Brahman", "Telyavelic Tremere",
					"Old Clan Tzimisce", "Gargoyles (Modern)", "Gargoyles (Scout)", "Gargoyles (Sentinel)",
					"Gargoyles (Warrior)", "Ventrue Antitribu", "Wu Zao", "Angellis Ater", "Maeghar", "Panders", "Caitiff",
					"Children of Osiris",
				},
				-- The revenant families (SPEC R93, I29b). A list of its OWN, not an alias and not an
				-- append: clan and family are two lists because the clan picker is going to be shown
				-- somewhere else WITHOUT the families, and only the ghoul dropdown wants both at once.
				--
				-- No empty item here - the empty one comes from `clan`, which leads the union.
				-- TWO names carry an era, and they split on DIFFERENT axes. Bratovich splits on the
				-- TRIO: Dark Ages has Potence where Modern has Fortitude. Grimaldi splits on the
				-- WEAKNESS, which is the second axis R93 never compared - the trio is the same
				-- Celerity/Dominate/Fortitude in both books, but da p.454 caps the family at eight
				-- blood points and gr p.98 gives it a behavioural flaw with no number in it at all
				-- (SPEC R129, I108b, the user 2026-08-28).
				--
				-- Obertus was re-read on 2026-08-28 (SPEC T786, Q17) and does NOT split by era: the trio
				-- matches in both books, and the weakness diverges only in WHICH Derangement - da p.454
				-- says Obsession, gr p.102 says Obsessive-Compulsive - which this sheet does not model,
				-- because a Derangement here is a box the player types into.
				--
				-- What the re-read DID turn up is a third kind of variant: a LINE inside a family.
				-- gr p.102 - "Obertus revenants, who display signs of the Narov line, should swap
				-- Obfuscate for Dominate." That is a CONDITION and not a free pick, so it is carried as
				-- its own entry rather than as a choice slot: a choice slot would hand Dominate to any
				-- Obertus, which is permission the book does not give. The shape is the one
				-- Gargoyles (Scout)/(Sentinel)/(Warrior) already set (Q21, the user 2026-08-28).
				["family"] = {
					"Basarab", "Bratovich (Dark Ages)", "Bratovitch (Modern)", "D'Habi", "Danislav",
					"Ducheski", "Enrathi", "Grimaldi (Dark Ages)", "Grimaldi (Modern)",
					"Kairouan Brotherhood", "Katayama", "Keskinen",
					"Khavi", "Krevcheski", "Marijava", "Obertus", "Obertus (Narov)", "Oprichniki",
					"Rafastio", "Rossellini",
					"Servants of Anushin-Rawan", "Szantovich", "Vlaszy", "Zantosa",
				},
				-- The morality roster (SPEC I99c). 55 rows, GENERATED from research/road_bearing.tsv,
				-- which is the MEASURED source: the three R rows are what was known before it.
				--
				-- `Humanity` leads and is NOT the empty item - a character without a road IS on Humanity,
				-- so there is no empty road to clear back to (SPEC C, the declared V15 exception).
				--
				-- `values` carries all 55 in every era; only the `items` filter, on the ROAD_ERA axis
				-- further down (SPEC I99c2) - the second axis V24 already declares. Names collide with
				-- other lists ON PURPOSE: `The Path of Blood` is BOTH a road and a Thaumaturgy path,
				-- which is trap 5 of research/README.md. Separate lists in separate places, and the one
				-- .lang key serves both because both read `A Trilha do Sangue`.
				["road"] = {
					"Humanity", "The Path of Blood", "The Path of the Bones", "The Path of Caine", "The Path of Cathari",
					"The Path of the Feral Heart", "The Path of Honorable Accord", "The Path of Lilith",
					"The Path of Metamorphosis", "The Path of Night", "The Path of Paradox",
					"The Path of Power and the Inner Voice", "The Path of Typhon", "The Path of the Hive",
					"The Path of the Scorched Heart", "The Path of Self-Focus", "The Path of Asakku",
					"The Path of Entelechy", "The Path of Ecstasy", "The Path of the Warrior", "Road of the Beast",
					"Road of Heaven", "Road of Humanity", "Road of Kings", "Road of Lilith", "Road of Metamorphosis",
					"Road of Sin", "Road of Bones", "Road of Yasa", "Road of Blood", "Road of Paradox",
					"The Code of Samiel", "Road of the Abyss", "Road of Set", "Path of the Archangel",
					"Road of Angra Mainyu", "Road of Ahura Mazda", "Path of the Hunter", "Path of Journeys",
					"Path of Liberation", "Path of Christianity", "Path of Life/Judaism", "Path of Breath",
					"Path of Community", "Path of Illumination", "Path of Chivalry", "Path of Devaraja", "Path of Daena",
					"Path of Thorns", "Path of Veils", "Path of Making", "Path of Pleasure", "Path of the Devil",
					"Path of Screams", "Path of Watchful Gods",
				},
				["nature"] = {
					"", "Activist", "Architect", "Autocrat", "Benefactor", "Bon Vivant", "Bravo", "Bureaucrat", "Caregiver",
					"Celebrant", "Chameleon", "Child", "Comedian", "Competitor", "Conformist", "Conniver", "Contrary",
					"Creep Show", "Critic", "Crusader", "Curmudgeon", "Dabbler", "Defender", "Deviant", "Director", "Enigma",
					"Explorer", "Eye of the Storm", "Fanatic", "Follower", "Gallant", "Gambler", "Grifter", "Guru", "Hacker",
					"Idealist", "Innovator", "Jester", "Judge", "Leader", "Loner", "Machine", "Mad Scientist", "Martyr",
					"Masochist", "Mediator", "Mercenary", "Monster", "Optimist", "Pedagogue", "Penitent", "Perfectionist",
					"Philosopher", "Pragmatist", "Prophet", "Rebel", "Rogue", "Sadist", "Samaritan", "Scientist",
					"Sensualist", "Soldier", "Survivor", "Thrill-Seeker", "Traditionalist", "Trendsetter", "Trickster",
					"Tyrant", "Visionary",
				},
				["speciality"] = {
					"", "Strength", "Dexterity", "Stamina", "Charisma", "Manipulation", "Appearance", "Perception",
					"Inteligence", "Wits", "Academics", "Alertness", "Animal Ken", "Archery", "Arts", "Athletics",
					"Awareness", "Brawl", "Commerce", "Computer", "Cosmology", "Crafts", "Drive", "Empathy", "Enigmas",
					"Esoterica", "Etiquette", "Expression", "Finance", "Firearms", "Hearth Wisdom", "Intimidation",
					"Investigation", "Larceny", "Law", "Leadership", "Legerdemain", "Martial Arts", "Medicine",
					"Meditation", "Melee", "Occult", "Performance", "Philosophy", "Politics", "Religion", "Research",
					"Ride", "Ritual", "Science", "Seneschal", "Stealth", "Streetwise", "Subterfuge", "Survival",
					"Technology", "Theology",
				},
				-- Forty-seven items since T764, which MEASURED where each name is defined and wrote
				-- research/bg_essence.tsv. TWO names carry an origin suffix because their games do
				-- not share a mechanic: `Status` (V20 p.118 is standing among the Kindred, M20
				-- p.325 is respect among Awakened peers) and `Totem` (M20 p.326 is a personal pact
				-- with a spirit, W20 p.140 is a PACK trait the whole pack pools its points into).
				-- Every other cross-game homonym (Allies, Contacts, Fame, Influence, Library,
				-- Mentor, Rank, Requisitions, Resources, Retainers) reads the same in every book -
				-- `Resources` repeats the sentence word for word in V20 p.115 and W20 p.138 - and
				-- stays ONE item: a suffix there would separate nothing (SPEC I105b).
				["background"] = {
					"", "Allies", "Alternate Identity", "Ancestors", "Arcane", "Armory", "Artifacts", "Avatar", "Backup",
					"Base of Operations", "Certification", "Chantry", "Contacts", "Cult", "Demesne", "Destiny", "Domain",
					"Dream", "Enhancement", "Fame", "Familiar", "Fetish", "Generation", "Guide", "Herd", "Influence",
					"Kinfolk", "Legend", "Library", "Mentor", "Node", "Past Lives", "Patron", "Pure Breed", "Rank",
					"Requisitions", "Resources", "Retainers", "Rites", "Rituals", "Sanctum", "Secret Weapons", "Spies",
					"Status (Mage)", "Status (Vampire)", "Totem (Mage)", "Totem (Werewolf)", "Wonder",
				},
				-- Twenty-seven hedge paths since the 94th round, when the three books were swept whole
				-- and six the sheet did not carry came back with a page each (SPEC I69, R106, R107, R108).
				-- `Ephemera` still stands BEFORE `Enchantment`: the list inherited that from the book's own
				-- contents page and reordering it is a change nobody asked for - the six new ones take their
				-- alphabetical place and that one exception stays.
				["numina"] = {
					"", "Alchemy", "Chronomancy", "Conjuration", "Conveyance", "Curses", "Divination", "Dowsing",
					"Ephemera", "Enchantment", "Fascination", "Fortune", "Healing", "Hellfire", "Illusion",
					"Maelstroms", "Necromancy", "Necronics", "Oneiromancy", "Quintessence Manipulation", "Shadows",
					"Shapeshifting", "Spirit-Chasing", "Starlight", "Summoning, Binding, and Warding",
					"Via Geniorum", "Via Necromantiae", "Weather Control",
				},
				["psychic"] = {
					"", "Animal Psychics", "Anti-Psychic", "Astral Projection", "Biocontrol", "Channeling", "Clairvoyance",
					"Cyberkinesis", "Cyberpathy", "Ectoplasmic Generation", "Mind Shields", "Precognition",
					"Psychic Healing", "Psychic Hypnosis", "Psychic Invisibility", "Psychic Vampirism", "Psychokinesis",
					"Psychometry", "Psychoportation", "Pyrokinesis", "Shadow", "Synergy", "Telepathy",
				},
				-- The twenty-six affiliations a hedge magician can belong to, and it is a PICKER
				-- of prose like every other name on this sheet (SPEC I66, I27). The key is
				-- `hedgeAffiliation` and not `affiliation`: fieldRoot drops the "cbo" and
				-- lowercases the FIRST letter only, so cboHedgeAffiliation resolves here. A wrong
				-- key is not a compile error - it falls through to `or c.values`, which T493
				-- emptied, and the dropdown opens blank with rdk exiting 0 (SPEC V211a, B6).
				--
				-- Sorted by the WHOLE string, so the fourteen that open with `The` group under T,
				-- exactly as mainPath already does. `Lone Practitioner` is the BOOK's term for the
				-- unaffiliated (M20 Sorcerer p. 79) and is a choice of its own: the empty first
				-- item means "not answered yet" and the two are not the same state, though the
				-- filters of I67/I68 prune nothing for either (SPEC V15, V270c).
				["hedgeAffiliation"] = {
					"", "Balamo’ob", "Followers of Set", "Forn Jafnaðr", "Giovanni", "Lone Practitioner",
					"Maison Liban", "Mogen HaLev", "Nebuu-Afef, The Order of The Golden Fly", "Path-Dancers",
					"Thal’hun", "The Ancient Order of The Aeon Rites", "The Arcanum", "The Children of Osiris",
					"The Crystal Circle", "The Cult of Isis", "The Cult of Mercury",
					"The Dozen Priests of the Pythian Order", "The Fenian", "The Nephite Priesthood",
					"The Seven Thunders", "The Silver Portal",
					"The Society of Enlightened Altruistic Ideologies (SEAI)", "The Society of Leopold",
					"The Star Council", "U.S. Government (Project Twilight)", "Uzoma",
				},
				-- `faith` was a list of four religions until the 90th round, when the row became a
				-- typed field (SPEC I61, user 2026-08-23). It is gone rather than kept dormant:
				-- a PICKER_LIST key with no cbo* reading it is the dead data B55 cost a whole
				-- round of research to find. The four `wod.` keys stay in the .lang - nothing
				-- reprimands an unused key, and `Other` has other readers.
				-- The attribute a hedge magician casts on (SPEC I60). It is the same NINE names
				-- XP_ATTRS carries below, and the gate compares the two lists in BOTH directions
				-- for the reason V148 does it for the trait picker: an attribute that entered one
				-- side only would pass every count check on the sheet. `Inteligence` is the
				-- sheet's own spelling and has been since SPEC I3 - correcting it here alone
				-- would break the bijection, not fix a typo.
				["hedgeAttr"] = {
					"", "Strength", "Dexterity", "Stamina", "Charisma", "Manipulation", "Appearance",
					"Perception", "Inteligence", "Wits",
				},
				-- The rituals of static magic, and the list opens EMPTY on purpose: the powers are
				-- entered in a round of their own (user 2026-08-23, SPEC I65). The key still has to
				-- exist - pickerItems falls back to c.values when it finds none, and the box would
				-- come up outside the axis that translates it, which is B57 through another door
				-- (SPEC V269e). The empty first item is V15's, the same one every picker opens with.
				["hedgeRitual"] = {
					"",
					"1. Death Curse",
					"1. Deathsight",
					"1. Eldritch Mark",
					"1. Face Theft",
					"1. Healing Slumber",
					"1. Lifting Shadows",
					"1. Sprint",
					"1. Symbol Interpretation",
