			-- BLOOD_SORCERY (SPEC I18), RITUAL_DISC (SPEC I19) and ADVANCED_DISC. Dormant like
			-- CLANS above: no reader yet. The pickers get their items in SPEC T460, the guards
			-- arrive in T439/T440, and nothing reads ADVANCED_DISC at all - it is banked for a
			-- later round (user, 57th) and deliberately changes NOTHING on the sheet.
			--
			-- Membership in "blood sorcery" is DERIVED, never listed (SPEC V191): a Discipline is one
			-- iff it owns a path here or a ritual below. That lands on the seven SPEC R87 froze -
			-- Dark Thaumaturgy by paths alone, Abyss Mysticism by rituals alone (its MAIN PATHS box
			-- stays empty, which is the case SPEC I19 predicted).
			--
			-- Path names are the MODERN spelling wherever the same path exists in both eras, because
			-- the value is what gets saved and the era only changes the display (SPEC V24, I22). So
			-- Lure of Flames, not Creatio Ignis; The Way of the Spirit, not Genius Loci. The two
			-- Dark-Ages-only Thaumaturgy paths keep their Latin names - nothing modern to defer to.
			--
			-- A ritual can have MORE THAN ONE owner (user, 57th round), so every RITUAL_DISC value is
			-- a LIST even when it holds one name - one shape, so a reader never type-checks. Thirteen
			-- of the 284 carry two: the eight the core (p. 440) hands Assamite Sorcery under its own
			-- names, the four the Dark Ages files under Assamite and Setite clan rituals, and
			-- Mirror of Blood, which Rites of Blood prints as "Thaumaturgy or Koldunic". A ritual with
			-- two owners is offered under both, which is what the books mean by listing it twice.
			--
			-- Ritual levels run 1..9, not 1..5. Abyss Mysticism is the only Discipline that goes past
			-- five (Dark Ages pp. 273-274 and Tome of Secrets p. 38), and it does so because its
			-- rituals ARE its power ladder - it has no paths to spend the dots on.
			--
			-- ADVANCED_DISC is the sixth-to-ninth dot of a Discipline: elder powers, one entry per
			-- power as {level, name}, from the core Disciplines chapter plus its bloodline chapter
			-- and from Dark Ages p. 188 onward. Levels 6..9 by definition - the fifth dot and below
			-- is the ordinary ladder and is not repeated here. The sheet still draws five dots per
			-- Discipline row; this table does not ask it to draw more.
			local BLOOD_SORCERY = {
				-- >>> BLOOD_SORCERY_BEGIN (generated - SPEC T435)
